Yes, the image is highly relevant to the research presented in both PDFs. Both papers investigate Nano-11 nanoparticles as vaccine adjuvants, with a central mechanism being Nano-11's ability to enhance antigen uptake by dendritic cells (DCs). The image directly supports this by demonstrating significantly increased ovalbumin (OVA) uptake by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) when OVA is complexed with Nano-11, compared to soluble OVA alone. This in vitro evidence underpins the papers' claims that Nano-11 serves as an effective antigen delivery vehicle, crucial for augmenting the immune response.